cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use EuConform, its evidence format or its evaluation methods in your
  work, please cite it using the metadata below.
title: "EuConform: Open-Source Evidence Toolkit for AI Compliance"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Benedikt
    family-names: Hiepler
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-2068-0415"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Hiepler/EuConform"
url: "https://euconform.eu"
abstract: >-
  EuConform defines an open evidence format for AI compliance under the EU AI
  Act and provides offline, vendor-independent tools to produce, validate and
  empirically evaluate it: report, AI BOM, CI and bundle artifacts, schema
  validation, bundle verification, local bias evaluation with sentence
  log-probabilities, and CycloneDX interoperability.
keywords:
  - EU AI Act
  - AI compliance
  - Annex IV
  - evidence format
  - AI BOM
  - bias evaluation
  - model evaluation
  - offline-first
license:
  - MIT
  - EUPL-1.2
